  "description": "A short civic park crossing with a two-walking-tile gold-railed civic pond bridge with flared bank passing spaces, native roses and benches. The east promenade bends around a north-connected elm tongue toward the picnic gate; compact tree shoulders keep the crossing distinct from its garden turnouts. A trainer controls the short west paved lane; a longer nursery-grass walk bypasses the challenge in either direction. The fenced waterbody has visible closed northern and southern banks; the actual Mississippi remains a separate native channel south of this park.",
